DAT
id=qid::label=str::text=lstr::
21789::$$$message_0170_0000_0000$$$::[font italic=true]...What about the past?[font italic=false][lr]::
21790::$$$message_0170_0000_0001$$$::I'm curious what he thinks about the current situation, but I'm also curious about what he thinks about the past.[lr]::
21791::$$$message_0170_0000_0002$$$::Saber has a strong sense of discipline.[lr]::
21792::$$$message_0170_0000_0003$$$::Lancer may have some regrets from the past despite how cool he plays it.::
21793::$$$message_0170_0001_0000$$$::"Regrets? Little annoyances, sure, but well, I don't have any regrets."[wvs][se storage=se545.wav][lr]::
21794::$$$message_0170_0001_0001$$$::And thus...[lr]::
21795::$$$message_0170_0001_0002$$$::This rather underestimated hero of Ireland replies, all while staring at his underperforming fishing rod.::
21796::$$$message_0170_0002_0000$$$::"...I thought so. You really are frank. Other Servants tend to be homesick at the end of the day."::
21797::$$$message_0170_0003_0000$$$::"Heh, really now? They don't seem like the kind of folks that'd be looking for some magnificent return.[lr]::
21798::$$$message_0170_0003_0001$$$::...Oh, Caster has plenty of regrets, huh?[lr]::
21799::$$$message_0170_0003_0002$$$::She's originally a sheltered princess; I'm sure she's happier shut away in a castle. That would be better for you and the world's sake."::
21800::$$$message_0170_0004_0000$$$::Lancer yawns.[lr]::
21801::$$$message_0170_0004_0001$$$::He must either be unhappy that he isn't getting any strikes, or he doesn't like talking about the past.[lr]::
21802::$$$message_0170_0004_0002$$$::Regardless, he couldn't be bothered any more.::
21803::$$$message_0170_0005_0000$$$::"So, say you obtain the Holy Grail. Do you not have any wishes? Like getting a second life as a human or going back to the past?"[lr]::
21804::$$$message_0170_0005_0001$$$::"Who knows? I can't think of anything like that until the time comes."::
21805::$$$message_0170_0006_0000$$$::This is how he is.[lr]::
21806::$$$message_0170_0006_0001$$$::He's the type that's hand-to-mouth.[lr]::
21807::$$$message_0170_0006_0002$$$::He gets most of what we wants while he's alive. There's no way he leaves any regrets over what he should've done after the party is over.::
21808::$$$message_0170_0007_0000$$$::"The life of a hero, I guess... Oh, [wsplinemove canskip=0][splinemove textoff=0 opacity=255 layer=base time=400 path=(9,86,2.000)(295,111,2.000)(533,164,2.000) storage=fd25_ts accel=-2]yeah.[wsplinemove canskip=0][lr]::
21809::$$$message_0170_0007_0001$$$::Hey, Lancer. If you don't mind, can you tell me your story? Come to think of it, I don't know much about your tale."::
21810::$$$message_0170_0008_0000$$$::"Huh? You won't gain anything from it now even if you listen to something like that. Or what, are you guys actually trying to fight?"::
21811::$$$message_0170_0009_0000$$$::"No, Saber and I have no intention to fight.[lr]::
21812::$$$message_0170_0009_0001$$$::Didn't I say that I appreciate that you don't try to start stuff?"::
21813::$$$message_0170_0010_0000$$$::"Oh... I feel like I might've heard that. Well, if you say so, then you're probably right.[lr]::
21814::$$$message_0170_0010_0001$$$::So, what? Do you simply want to hear the story of another person's life?"[lr]::
21815::$$$message_0170_0010_0002$$$::"Yeah. Nothing shady about it, I'm just curious."::
21816::$$$message_0170_0011_0000$$$::"...Fine.[lr]::
21817::$$$message_0170_0011_0001$$$::I have no strikes, so I guess I can kill some time. I also had something I wanted to hammer into your head."[lr]::
21818::$$$message_0170_0011_0002$$$::Before, Lancer's expression seemed uninterested and dull, but something changed.[lr]::
21819::$$$message_0170_0011_0003$$$::His relaxed shoulders somehow slacken even further, while his gaze turns from the sea to lazily stare up at the sky.[lr]::
21820::$$$message_0170_0011_0004$$$::In other words, he got even more unmotivated.::
21821::$$$message_0170_0012_0000$$$::Lancer.[lr]::
21822::$$$message_0170_0012_0001$$$::Cú Chulainn is a hero talked about in ancient Ireland.[lr]::
21823::$$$message_0170_0012_0002$$$::His land is divided into five countries, and Cú Chulainn is a warrior who served the king of northern Ulster, King Conchobar.[lr]::
21824::$$$message_0170_0012_0003$$$::Since it is a Celtic myth, few here in Japan know of it, but he is a great hero who surpasses King Arthur in his homeland.::
21825::$$$message_0170_0013_0000$$$::His birth is rather complicated.[lr]::
21826::$$$message_0170_0013_0001$$$::Cú Chulainn's mother, Deichtire, is a princess born to Maga, the consort of King Ross the Red, and a certain outstanding druid.[lr]::
21827::$$$message_0170_0013_0002$$$::Princess Deichtire disappeared to Tír na nÓg without marrying anyone and had a baby with the sun god, Lugh, while there.[lr]::
21828::$$$message_0170_0013_0003$$$::The baby was Sétanta[line len=2]who would later be called Cú Chulainn.::
21829::$$$message_0170_0014_0000$$$::Sétanta was sent to be a shield to Ulster by joining King Conchobar's army and was to live a life just as his fate suggests.::
21830::$$$message_0170_0015_0000$$$::Sétanta started getting called Cú Chulainn from when he accidentally killed the guard dog of Culann, the swordsmith, when he was still a boy.::
21831::$$$message_0170_0016_0000$$$::One day, King Conchobar was invited to the house of Culann, the famous swordsmith.[lr]::
21832::$$$message_0170_0016_0001$$$::The king tried to bring Sétanta, who was still a boy, but Sétanta was in the middle of a hurling match with his friends.[lr]::
21833::$$$message_0170_0016_0002$$$::"If I were to withdraw now, I would lose the match. I will catch up once I win the match, so please go ahead."[lr]::
21834::$$$message_0170_0016_0003$$$::The king, pleased by the boy's words, allowed him to come later and headed to Culann's house first.::
21835::$$$message_0170_0017_0000$$$::The misfortune started from when Culann's servant accidentally closed the gate out of carelessness.[lr]::
21836::$$$message_0170_0017_0001$$$::Sétanta, who arrived late, was attacked by the guard dog, so he strangled it to death.[lr]::
21837::$$$message_0170_0017_0002$$$::All those inside the house gathered after hearing the commotion. Upon learning that Sétanta defeated the guard dog, everyone was surprised and praised him.::
21838::$$$message_0170_0018_0000$$$::But there was some sadness in Culann's eyes from losing his prized guard dog. Sétanta, ashamed of his thoughtlessness, told him: ::
21839::$$$message_0170_0019_0000$$$::"Does this dog have an offspring? If so, let me care for them. I will raise one to become an excellent guard dog that rivals their father. Until then, I shall be your guard dog."[lr]::
21840::$$$message_0170_0019_0001$$$::Culann, the swordsmith, was impressed by the boy's offer and replied with conviction.::
21841::$$$message_0170_0020_0000$$$::"No need for that. I will raise a guard dog that will protect this house. You train yourself. Eventually, you will without a doubt become the guard dog that protects all of Ulster."[lr]::
21842::$$$message_0170_0020_0001$$$::All of the warriors who gathered nodded in agreement.::
21843::$$$message_0170_0021_0000$$$::Thereafter, the boy would be called "Cú Chulainn," or Culann's guard dog.[lr]::
21844::$$$message_0170_0021_0001$$$::The boy's first battle.[lr]::
21845::$$$message_0170_0021_0002$$$::In honor of the noble offer that followed.::
21846::$$$message_0170_0022_0000$$$::"I knew that much, but... How old were you at that time?"[lr]::
21847::$$$message_0170_0022_0001$$$::"I was younger than you are now. I wasn't a warrior yet. In our country, there was a training group for children before becoming a Knight of the Red Branch. It was a gathering of apprentice youth warriors, and I was one of them."::
21848::$$$message_0170_0023_0000$$$::"Man. So what, you strangled the best guard dog in the country at like twelve or thirteen?"[lr]::
21849::$$$message_0170_0023_0001$$$::"It was the adrenaline. It was my first time taking a life. Since then, it became my Geas to never eat a dog though."[lr]::
21850::$$$message_0170_0023_0002$$$::I don't know how serious he is, but he cracks a cannibalism joke.::
21851::$$$message_0170_0024_0000$$$::"So, it was a while after my name had changed. The group of apprentices gathered under one druid and were making a ruckus asking him to predict whether they will receive good fate once they become a warrior.[lr]::
21852::$$$message_0170_0024_0001$$$::That druid was, well, an old man that had rather strong powers. So his fortunes were more like 'deciding the future' than 'seeing the future.' The old man was troubled and decided to only fortune-tell those who would become a warrior that day."::
21853::$$$message_0170_0025_0000$$$::"I see. So, what were the results?"[lr]::
21854::$$$message_0170_0025_0001$$$::"It was so bad, none of the other apprentice knights tried to go through the rites of warriorhood."[lr]::
21855::$$$message_0170_0025_0002$$$::"...Hm. What were you doing?"[lr]::
21856::$$$message_0170_0025_0003$$$::"I wasn't interested, so I was leaning against a hazel tree and fishing."[lr]::
21857::$$$message_0170_0025_0004$$$::"...Sorry. What was the point of that story?"::
21858::$$$message_0170_0026_0000$$$::"You don't get it?[lr]::
21859::$$$message_0170_0026_0001$$$::In other words, I went through the rites of warriorhood that day.[lr]::
21860::$$$message_0170_0026_0002$$$::The king was furious. Saying like, 'why would a child like you become a warrior? You should grow up healthily until you're mature' or something.[lr]::
21861::$$$message_0170_0026_0003$$$::That got me pissed, so I broke all the spears in the castle, destroyed a chariot, and threatened him."::
21862::$$$message_0170_0027_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
21863::$$$message_0170_0027_0001$$$::H-he threatened the king? Has this man actually gotten a lot more mellow than before?[lr]::
21864::$$$message_0170_0027_0002$$$::According to Saber, he has an affinity with the Berserker class, but I didn't actually think that was true.::
21865::$$$message_0170_0028_0000$$$::"So that's how you became a warrior, huh?[lr]::
21866::$$$message_0170_0028_0001$$$::...Um, was it the Knights of the Red Branch?"::
21867::$$$message_0170_0029_0000$$$::"Yeah. If you ask Saber, it's nothing like her chivalry.[lr]::
21868::$$$message_0170_0029_0001$$$::After all, as long as you're not disloyal, you can fight as you wish.[lr]::
21869::$$$message_0170_0029_0002$$$::It's common to pick a fight in another territory if you feel like it, hold a party that night, and then forget about it.[lr]::
21870::$$$message_0170_0029_0003$$$::My order was full of dumbasses, so I couldn't let my guard down in my own country more than other countries."::
21871::$$$message_0170_0030_0000$$$::He laughs. It must really be that funny to him.[lr]::
21872::$$$message_0170_0030_0001$$$::...I see. His free-spirited nature is the difference in the world that he survived through.[lr]::
21873::$$$message_0170_0030_0002$$$::That pride is not complicated like a human's, but simple like a beast's.::
21874::$$$message_0170_0031_0000$$$::"So, I fought day and night once I became a warrior.[lr]::
21875::$$$message_0170_0031_0001$$$::I fell in love at first sight with one of those princesses, so I went to the castle to kidnap her. She was a real sharp woman, though.[lr]::
21876::$$$message_0170_0031_0002$$$::She said she didn't feel like going with some kid with no reputation."[lr]::
21877::$$$message_0170_0031_0003$$$::"Wait. Kid? How old were you then?"::
21878::$$$message_0170_0032_0000$$$::"Oh, I think I was around sixteen. So, I went out on a journey in search of glory.[lr]::
21879::$$$message_0170_0032_0001$$$::There was this warrior woman named Scáthach in this place called the Land of Shadows who was apparently as strong as a monster. Rumor had it that she had many warriors as apprentices."::
21880::$$$message_0170_0033_0000$$$::I know the rest.[lr]::
21881::$$$message_0170_0033_0001$$$::Cú Chulainn reached the Land of Shadows, known as a place infested with demons, and received the demonic spear, Gáe Bolg, and the leaping secrets of the female lord, Scáthach.::
21882::$$$message_0170_0034_0000$$$::"You say it like it's easy. Her intensity would make your little lady Tohsaka run away barefoot if she had to.[lr]::
21883::$$$message_0170_0034_0001$$$::Anyway, she was crazy and had already thrown away her humanity by the time I arrived. See, the Land of Shadows is, well, a territory of the afterlife. That woman had become the guard to lay into the ghosts there."::
21884::$$$message_0170_0035_0000$$$::"There were some god-like fellas amongst those ghosts.[lr]::
21885::$$$message_0170_0035_0001$$$::She was able to take 'em to task with her spear handling as a human, so you ought to be able to figure how insane she was, eh?"::
21886::$$$message_0170_0036_0000$$$::"Yeah. It scares me to imagine something like a powered up version of Tohsaka."[lr]::
21887::$$$message_0170_0036_0001$$$::"Right. So, there were other apprentices under that scary teacher.[lr]::
21888::$$$message_0170_0036_0002$$$::They were all warriors who came to learn under Scáthach, but there was one who was my equal.[lr]::
21889::$$$message_0170_0036_0003$$$::He was called Ferdiad. A warrior from the neighboring country, Connacht. While we were fighting each other over the Gáe Bolg, we had exchanged oaths of brotherhood before I knew it."::
21890::$$$message_0170_0037_0000$$$::"...Well, how should I say it.[lr]::
21891::$$$message_0170_0037_0001$$$::I had three priceless best friends, but he was like a special older brother figure to me even among them."::
21892::$$$message_0170_0038_0000$$$::Cú Chulainn then learned all kinds of techniques and magecraft.[lr]::
21893::$$$message_0170_0038_0001$$$::...But wow. I didn't think that all of the heroic tales that I knew were carried out when he was sixteen.[lr]::
21894::$$$message_0170_0038_0002$$$::From what I've heard, it seems like this guy was going on a rampage at full speed everyday.[lr]::
21895::$$$message_0170_0038_0003$$$::Like a swift horse, living fast and recklessly.::
21896::$$$message_0170_0039_0000$$$::"That's not true. I was living in the Land of Shadows for a while.[lr]::
21897::$$$message_0170_0039_0001$$$::It was comfortable since I had a good teacher and a good rival.[lr]::
21898::$$$message_0170_0039_0002$$$::So then, this idiot came to disrupt that comfort. Aífe, a lord from a neighboring country, started a war.[lr]::
21899::$$$message_0170_0039_0003$$$::Scáthach for some reason didn't want to send me to the battlefield, and we argued many times."::
21900::$$$message_0170_0040_0000$$$::"Well, in the end, Scáthach, Ferdiad, and I went on a tear alongside each other and captured Aífe alive after a single combat.[lr]::
21901::$$$message_0170_0040_0001$$$::But well, how do I put it? At first, she was a detestable enemy. But once we captured her, I realized she was also a fine woman.[lr]::
21902::$$$message_0170_0040_0002$$$::So I was serious, but Scáthach found out and threw stones at me. Gáe Bolg style."::
21903::$$$message_0170_0041_0000$$$::Lancer lets out a nervous laugh amidst his reverie. [lr]::
21904::$$$message_0170_0041_0001$$$::I see, so the enemy lord was this woman[line len=2]::
21905::$$$message_0170_0042_0000$$$::"Hold on. That's what you meant when you said you were serious!?"[lr]::
21906::$$$message_0170_0042_0001$$$::"Of course. If I fall in love, it's obvious I'm going to sleep with her."[lr]::
21907::$$$message_0170_0042_0002$$$::"Gah."[lr]::
21908::$$$message_0170_0042_0003$$$::...That's right. Great heroes are great lovers. But man, these warriors sure have no inhibitions!::
21909::$$$message_0170_0043_0000$$$::"But the time for farewell always comes.[lr]::
21910::$$$message_0170_0043_0001$$$::I broke up with Aífe too. If she bore my child, I asked her to name him Connla and send him to Ulster. I also gave him three vows to follow.[lr]::
21911::$$$message_0170_0043_0002$$$::First, do not answer even if you are asked for your name.[lr]::
21912::$$$message_0170_0043_0003$$$::Second, do not change your chosen path no matter what.[lr]::
21913::$$$message_0170_0043_0004$$$::Third, do not decline when challenged to fight.[lr]::
21914::$$$message_0170_0043_0005$$$::Well, those are the minimum requirements for my son."::
21915::$$$message_0170_0044_0000$$$::"So, Ferdiad and I left the Land of Shadows the same day.[lr]::
21916::$$$message_0170_0044_0001$$$::When I left the castle, we both asked each other, 'Would you want to come to my country?' [wvl canskip=0 time=400][clfg][dash page=back mx=0 opacity=255 layer=base irot=-0.0 cx=463 imag=2 time=100 cy=73 mag=2 my=0 storage=fd25_01e rot=-0.0 accel=0][transex standard=fore time=300]We both laughed, realizing that neither of us would back down.[lr]::
21917::$$$message_0170_0044_0002$$$::As for Scáthach, well, I didn't see her on the day I left. I guess there was nothing left to say after teaching me everything."::
21918::$$$message_0170_0045_0000$$$::That was the story of the Land of Shadows.[lr]::
21919::$$$message_0170_0045_0001$$$::With that, Lancer goes silent for a bit.[lr]::
21920::$$$message_0170_0045_0002$$$::Returning to Ulster, Cú Chulainn was quite the conspicuous figure on the battlefield, and became a warrior known to all of Ireland in the blink of an eye.[lr]::
21921::$$$message_0170_0045_0003$$$::He achieved things in war nobody could replicate, came for the princess as promised while killing King Forgall and any troops that opposed him, and earned in battle with his fellow order members the title of the number one warrior of Ulster.::
21922::$$$message_0170_0046_0000$$$::His glorious career also marked the youth of the hero Cú Chulainn at the same time.::
21923::$$$message_0170_0047_0000$$$::After this...[lr]::
21924::$$$message_0170_0047_0001$$$::Cú Chulainn's fights would always bear a heavy shadow.::
21925::$$$message_0170_0048_0000$$$::"For generations, queens held power in the neighboring country of Connacht. Among them, Queen Medb was a competitive woman who loved war. Well, a lot happened and she marched on Ulster."[wm canskip=0]::
21926::$$$message_0170_0049_0000$$$::"First of all, one of the reasons Connacht invaded was because Uncle Fergus defected.[lr]::
21927::$$$message_0170_0049_0001$$$::Our king also had his issues, and well, the root cause was he killed Uncle Fergus's sons out of lust for a young woman."::
21928::$$$message_0170_0050_0000$$$::"...Hey. If memory serves, Princess Deichtire had you fostered, and Fergus was one of the knights to do so, right?"::
21929::$$$message_0170_0051_0000$$$::"Yeah. So my uncle, pride of the Knights of the Red Branch, served Connacht out of hatred for the King of Ulster.[lr]::
21930::$$$message_0170_0051_0001$$$::Uncle Fergus played a part in Queen Medb's aggression.[lr]::
21931::$$$message_0170_0051_0002$$$::On top of that, there was something of a curse on the people of Ulster. When another country invaded, all the men in the country became so weak that they couldn't fight."::
21932::$$$message_0170_0052_0000$$$::"Huh!?"[lr]::
21933::$$$message_0170_0052_0001$$$::[font italic=true]What the?[font italic=false][lr]::
21934::$$$message_0170_0052_0002$$$::[font italic=true]How did you prosper in that condition, Ireland!?[font italic=false]::
21935::$$$message_0170_0053_0000$$$::"W-w-[wvl][shock vmax=20 time=300 count=-2]what happened!? If they can't fight, they'd be looted and conquered in no time!"[lr]::
21936::$$$message_0170_0053_0001$$$::"It's like getting kicked when you're already down. But anyway, technically, I wasn't born in Ulster. I was born in a fairy mound. That's why I was the only one who was able to move freely."::
21937::$$$message_0170_0054_0000$$$::"You know the rest, right?[lr]::
21938::$$$message_0170_0054_0001$$$::Every day, we cut Medb's troops down like mowing grass. Once they started to see the writing on the wall, we agreed to continue the war in the form of single duels."::
21939::$$$message_0170_0055_0000$$$::"I fought in a duel in the ford of the Ulster gorge.[lr]::
21940::$$$message_0170_0055_0001$$$::I said that the Connacht army could advance only while I'm fighting in a duel.[lr]::
21941::$$$message_0170_0055_0002$$$::Either five thousand people are killed in a day, or they can slightly advance at the cost of one person.[lr]::
21942::$$$message_0170_0055_0003$$$::Medb reluctantly agreed and then my series of daily duels started."::
21943::$$$message_0170_0056_0000$$$::"Wow..."[lr]::
21944::$$$message_0170_0056_0001$$$::This is the so-called Cú Chulainn's Rune of vows.[lr]::
21945::$$$message_0170_0056_0002$$$::Ath nGabla, surrounded by four branches, that promises a duel with honor at stake.::
21946::$$$message_0170_0057_0000$$$::"Good idea.[lr]::
21947::$$$message_0170_0057_0001$$$::There's no way that Culann's guard dog would lose to a duel so that would hold back the Connacht army."::
21948::$$$message_0170_0058_0000$$$::"Nah, Medb broke the agreement and advanced.[lr]::
21949::$$$message_0170_0058_0001$$$::But well, it was a vow exchanged in front of many witnesses.[lr]::
21950::$$$message_0170_0058_0002$$$::So for the witnesses not to notice, only one unit advanced. Still, it was the best way to hold them back."::
21951::$$$message_0170_0059_0000$$$::"So, the problem was my duel.[lr]::
21952::$$$message_0170_0059_0001$$$::There were warriors that I thought were a waste, sending them to die at my hand. Then there was interference by a weirdo war goddess. And then there was Clan Calatin, the twenty-eight person monster. It was crazy. Hell, there was a time I slept a full day from fatigue.[lr]::
21953::$$$message_0170_0059_0002$$$::And, well, there was a point when the young guns of Ulster who weren't considered warriors yet banded together to try and help Cú Chulainn and ended up getting slaughtered by Medb. That's also on me, ultimately."::
21954::$$$message_0170_0060_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
21955::$$$message_0170_0060_0001$$$::I take it back.[lr]::
21956::$$$message_0170_0060_0002$$$::The fighting at the fords was a death trap even for the hero, Cú Chulainn.[lr]::
21957::$$$message_0170_0060_0003$$$::And at the end of this once-in-a-lifetime death trap...::
21958::$$$message_0170_0061_0000$$$::"The strongest warrior in Connacht.[lr]::
21959::$$$message_0170_0061_0001$$$::The only man that I did not want to fight in this world."[lr]::
21960::$$$message_0170_0061_0002$$$::The warrior he had trained with in the Land of Shadows.[lr]::
21961::$$$message_0170_0061_0003$$$::The duel with Ferdiad, who Cú Chulainn respected as an older brother figure.::
21962::$$$message_0170_0062_0000$$$::This fight was not Ferdiad's will, but one of Queen Medb's schemes.[lr]::
21963::$$$message_0170_0062_0001$$$::Lancer did not talk about how much of a dilemma both sides had.[lr]::
21964::$$$message_0170_0062_0002$$$::Both served their lords with their lives.[lr]::
21965::$$$message_0170_0062_0003$$$::In order to uphold their honor, less valuable to them than their friendship, they had to potentially throw away their lives.::
21966::$$$message_0170_0063_0000$$$::Their abilities were evenly matched, and a cornered Cú Chulainn struck Ferdiad's heart with Gáe Bolg.[lr]::
21967::$$$message_0170_0063_0001$$$::He released the demonic spear that he had not once used since the Land of Shadows on his irreplaceable best friend.::
21968::$$$message_0170_0064_0000$$$::"Gáe Bolg is the honor gifted to the greatest warrior."[lr]::
21969::$$$message_0170_0064_0001$$$::Cú Chulainn held his collapsed senior in his arms,[lr]::
21970::$$$message_0170_0064_0002$$$::"In that brilliant learning environment, [wait canskip=0 time=400]you were our pride..."[lr]::
21971::$$$message_0170_0064_0003$$$::and Ferdiad spoke his last to the world.::
21972::$$$message_0170_0065_0000$$$::...That battle ended with the defeat of the enemy country, Connacht.[lr]::
21973::$$$message_0170_0065_0001$$$::The Ulster warriors managed to recover from the cursed weakness they suffered and attacked the Connacht army, landing a devastating blow.[lr]::
21974::$$$message_0170_0065_0002$$$::After their battle, Cú Chulainn captured Queen Medb alive, but instead of killing her or shaming her, he is said to have returned her to Connacht with all due honor to a queen.::
21975::$$$message_0170_0066_0000$$$::"So you also let an enemy general go here too.[lr]::
21976::$$$message_0170_0066_0001$$$::...You've never killed a woman, huh?"[lr]::
21977::$$$message_0170_0066_0002$$$::"I guess so.[lr]::
21978::$$$message_0170_0066_0003$$$::It's not like I planned it like that, it really was a coincidence[line len=2]eh, but I guess I'm not fond of it, sure."::
21979::$$$message_0170_0067_0000$$$::That's not the problem.[lr]::
21980::$$$message_0170_0067_0001$$$::It doesn't matter whether you love them or hate them.[lr]::
21981::$$$message_0170_0067_0002$$$::Putting aside how he is as a Servant now, it means that Cú Chulainn as a hero didn't like killing women on a battlefield.::
21982::$$$message_0170_0068_0000$$$::"What about after that?"[lr]::
21983::$$$message_0170_0068_0001$$$::"There weren't any huge wars after that.[lr]::
21984::$$$message_0170_0068_0002$$$::Oh... Come to think of it, a weird kid came to the shore and started a ruckus.[lr]::
21985::$$$message_0170_0068_0003$$$::He was this brat that would beat the shit out of every warrior that tried to talk to him. Even the king took one look at him and decided only Cú Chulainn can defeat this child."::
21986::$$$message_0170_0069_0000$$$::"...The only times my princess tried to stop me was at that moment, and the one at the end of my life.[lr]::
21987::$$$message_0170_0069_0001$$$::She cried, saying that I mustn't go. But it was an order from the king and all, so, I had to suck it up anyway."::
21988::$$$message_0170_0070_0000$$$::"So, I fought with this kid at the shore, but he was so strong that I had no choice but to use Gáe Bolg.[lr]::
21989::$$$message_0170_0070_0001$$$::After I beat him, he said 'she didn't teach me that' before dying. He must've been Scáthach's apprentice.[lr]::
21990::$$$message_0170_0070_0002$$$::Yeah. And that kid's name was Connla."[lr]::
21991::$$$message_0170_0070_0003$$$::"..."::
21992::$$$message_0170_0071_0000$$$::That marks the end of the golden era for the hero, Cú Chulainn.[lr]::
21993::$$$message_0170_0071_0001$$$::The rest need not be said.[lr]::
21994::$$$message_0170_0071_0002$$$::Queen Medb sought revenge and so gathered fighters from far and wide with grudges against Cú Chulainn, all to corner him with all manner of wicked plots.[lr]::
21995::$$$message_0170_0071_0003$$$::And to defend the Ulster once more in their moment of weakness, he took on Medb's army alone, enduring countless traps, until he met a merciless end.::
21996::$$$message_0170_0072_0000$$$::He carried out many feats of valor. A great hero. The shield of Ulster.[lr]::
21997::$$$message_0170_0072_0001$$$::Compared to that glory, his life was surprisingly short.[lr]::
21998::$$$message_0170_0072_0002$$$::The guard dog of Culann was a warrior child who came to the end of his life as if running toward it.::
21999::$$$message_0170_0073_0000$$$::That is Cú Chulainn's story.[lr]::
22000::$$$message_0170_0073_0001$$$::It's almost sunset.[lr]::
22001::$$$message_0170_0073_0002$$$::For such an idle curiosity, this sure took up quite some time.::
22002::$$$message_0170_0074_0000$$$::"I'll start heading back. Thanks for the long story."[lr]::
22003::$$$message_0170_0074_0001$$$::Lancer snorts and faces away.[lr]::
22004::$$$message_0170_0074_0002$$$::He probably thinks this was a waste of time.::
22005::$$$message_0170_0075_0000$$$::"Oh yeah, I almost forgot.[lr]::
22006::$$$message_0170_0075_0001$$$::What was it that you wanted to hammer into my head?"::
22007::$$$message_0170_0076_0000$$$::"Can't you tell? It's that I didn't kill any women or lords."[lr]::
22008::$$$message_0170_0076_0001$$$::"Oh, I see."[lr]::
22009::$$$message_0170_0076_0002$$$::Cú Chulainn didn't give up a single command from the king during the many battles, no matter how reckless it was.[lr]::
22010::$$$message_0170_0076_0003$$$::His story also told that truth.::
22011::$$$message_0170_0077_0000$$$::"That was very helpful. I'll return this favor another time."[lr]::
22012::$$$message_0170_0077_0001$$$::"All right. Get some drinks from that Taiga girl for me, will you?"::
22013::$$$message_0170_0078_0000$$$::I leave the port.[lr]::
22014::$$$message_0170_0078_0001$$$::...Man, sorry for underestimating you.[lr]::
22015::$$$message_0170_0078_0002$$$::I didn't think they would make the first move at this point[line len=3]::
921922::$$$message_9170_0046_0000$$$::His glorious career also marked the youth of the hero Cú Chulainn at the same time.[r]����